@@ -1,3 +1,41 @@
+## Notes (1.3.5, FulDC++ build of 1.3.4)
+
+Not an upstream release: a build of 1.3.4 with safety fixes, published in the FulDC++ extension
+catalog. The behaviour fixes have tests (tests/) that fail on unpatched 1.3.4; the live-setting
+hooks, the menu filter and the error catching in main.ts were checked in a running client.
+
+- Redownloads download only a search result whose folder name matches exactly; they never fall
+  back to "the first result" (which merged unrelated folders into the release under its name).
+- Only proof starts a redownload: a file the SFV lists is missing or failed CRC, or the SFV is
+  unreadable. The "possibly missing" checks (SFV/NFO possibly missing, incomplete) only report.
+  Only real release folders are searched for; CD1/Sample/Subs resolve to their release, and share
+  roots or personal folders are never searched for. (1.3.4 started doing this for every new share
+  folder, so a personal mp3 folder could get someone else's content downloaded into it.)
+- A file that fails CRC is moved out of the share into the extension's "quarantine" folder
+  instead of deleted (this covers the whole share, where a retagged mp3 fails too), kept 30 days
+  with a note of where it came from; at most 20 per hour; accepted releases are left alone.
+- SFV files are never deleted; only an SFV with no valid lines is set aside (quarantine), and
+  only that starts a redownload, once per distinct broken SFV.
+- A release missing both a file and its NFO is still repaired (the proof decides, not the
+  order the checks finished in); lower-case scene names count as releases; symlinked files
+  count as present.
+- ".dctmp" partial files are no longer deleted (paused downloads lost their progress) nor
+  reported as extra files.
+- /rvalidator accept covers subfolders, cancels pending searches, and is respected by the CRC
+  handling and redownloads. Start-up cleanup no longer drops entries on a drive that is not
+  mounted yet. The list is saved atomically and a failed save is reported.
+- At most 30 redownload searches per hour and 200 waiting folders.
+- An unexpected error in a scan hook answers at once instead of making the client wait 60-120 s
+  (and then let the item through anyway). Start-up, command and menu errors are caught.
+- The two scan hooks follow their settings without a restart. The queue menu item's filter
+  answers from memory (the native GUI waits for it when the menu opens).
+- SFV reading: UTF-16 and ANSI (Windows-1252) files, ";" inside names, hexadecimal CRCs,
+  subfolder lines.
+- Scanning: junctions/symlinks are not followed, files vanishing mid-scan are not read errors,
+  Thumbs.db/desktop.ini/.DS_Store are not extra files. A relative or missing path for
+  /rvalidator scan is refused; one manual scan at a time.
+- Setting and menu texts say what actually happens.
+
